From dc87b43db16617e2c10b0942b7f070b3ba0ad2b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 14:05:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.4.1: AI Advisor Mode B (optional USB key) + clean
 two-build split

MODE B - optional USB physical key, additive to the arming code (never a
replacement). Off unless the user enrolls one.
- Enroll: router generates a 256-bit reaper.key onto the inserted stick and
  stores only its SHA-256 (rmcp_usb_hash); the key lives on the stick.
- Arm: when enrolled, arming also requires the matching stick present; the
  matched keyfile path is written into the session file.
- Removal locks the door: rmcpd stats the keyfile each tick and self-kills
  the instant the stick is pulled (mount vanishes). No hotplug wiring.
- httpd: usb_enroll/usb_unenroll actions + arm-time key check + status flag;
  GUI gains an optional USB-key card. nvram rmcp_usb_enable/rmcp_usb_hash.

TWO-BUILD SPLIT COMPLETENESS - the without-MCP image must carry ZERO MCP
trace, so close the non-C gaps left in v1.4.0:
- shared/defaults.c: the rmcp_* nvram block is now inside
  #ifdef RTCONFIG_REAPER_MCP (was unconditional).
- www/Makefile: when RTCONFIG_REAPER_MCP is off, delete Reaper_Advisor.asp
  and strip the AI-Advisor menu entry (menuTree.js, JS-comment markers) and
  the dashboard rail link (Main_ReaperDash.asp, matched by href - the
  minifier strips HTML comments so marker-based ranges do not survive there).
Verified by a full flag-off build: no rmcpd binary, no Advisor page, zero
menu/rail/rc/httpd/nvram MCP references, flag #undef in the header.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
